{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cfbf4FyQxjcpx7GALaqeU", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Use **structlog**. It's the project convention, and `structlog>=24.1` is already a dependency in `pyproject.toml`. Don't use the stdlib `logging` module.\n\nThe pattern, as in `src/billing/invoices.py`:\n\n```python\nimport structlog\n\nlog = structlog.get_logger()\n\nlog.info(\"invoice_created\", invoice_id=invoice.id, total=invoice.total)\n```\n\n- Create the logger at module level with `structlog.get_logger()`.\n- Use snake_case event names, like `invoice_created`.\n- Pass context as keyword arguments instead of formatting it into the message string."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1146, "cache_read_input_tokens": 24058, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1146}, "output_tokens": 202, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "9b85c114-68bd-4f37-89f6-ab74ae1e92fb", "uuid": "1655d899-a3d6-4581-991f-5d8ab3d4cf76", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T14:14:42.511Z", "request_id": "req_011Cfbf4Ei2M2Lc7EU3oATV3"}
